silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_02_pullback_as_constraint_validation_concrete_anchor#transportpullback silm:hasLongDescription "The TransportPullback is the pullback of the Vet-Imports-Household-Records functor. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F^*', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_02_pullback_as_constraint_validation_concrete_anchor#clinicbodymassrangeconstraint a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.03_pullback_vs_pushforward.sections.02_pullback_as_constraint_validation.concrete_anchor#clinicbodymassrangeconstraint" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_02_pullback_as_constraint_validation_concrete_anchor#clinicbodymassrangeconstraint silm:hasLongDescription "The ClinicBodyMassRangeConstraint is the clinic-side SHACL shape that asserts every body-mass is in [0.5, 10] kg. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'clinic SHACL shape', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
