silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_02_pullback_as_constraint_validation_concrete_anchor#householdadmissibilitycheck silm:hasLongDescription "The HouseholdAdmissibilityCheck is the household-side precondition: 'Mittens body-mass must be in [0.5, 10] kg before transport is admitted'. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'household-side check', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
